<h2>Why this playlist matters for programmers and developers</h2>
<p>Yes, Joe Rogan talks to people who do weird and wonderful things. No, you should not treat the JRE as ambient background noise while you write buggy code. This curated list pulls the episodes that actually teach something useful for programmers, software engineers, and anyone who pretends to love productivity hacks.</p>
<p>Expect mental models, systems thinking, attention hacks, and practical security advice. These are not crash courses in Python or Kubernetes. They are frameworks that help you design systems, debug hard problems, make career decisions, and stay sane while shipping features.</p>
